+    /// Open with an EXACT, controller-issued writer epoch (ADR-0012, V16
+    /// inv. 78-80).
+    ///
+    /// Upstream allocates the writer epoch internally as `stored + 1`. That
+    /// is observe-and-bind: the value is derived from what this process read,
+    /// so it cannot compose with a controller that is separately fencing the
+    /// same actor - both allocators race and the manifest keeps whichever
+    /// landed last. With this set, the controller decides the number and the
+    /// manifest either claims exactly it or returns `Fenced` before writing
+    /// anything, so replaying a spent epoch is refused rather than bumped
+    /// over.
